            <text>2.3.3.5 Funktionen umkehren [Invert functions]</text>
        </name>
        <questiontext format="html">
            <text><![CDATA[
<p class="HELM_exercise">
    <span class="multilang" lang="en">
        Exercise
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="de">
        Übung
    </span>
</p>
<p>
    <span class="multilang" lang="en">
        Find the inverse of each of the following functions:
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="de">
        Finden Sie die Umkehrung jeder der folgenden Funktionen:
    </span>
</p>
<ol class="HELM_parts">
    <li>
        <p>
            \(f(x)= {@aa@} \Rightarrow f^{-1}(x) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            \(f(x)= {@bb@} \Rightarrow f^{-1}(x) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            \(f(x)= {@cc@} \Rightarrow f^{-1}(x) = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            \(\displaystyle{f(x)= {@dd@} \Rightarrow f^{-1}(x) = }\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]
        </p>
    </li>
</ol>
]]></text>
        </questiontext>
        <generalfeedback format="html">
            <text><![CDATA[
<ol class="HELM_parts">
    <li>
        <p>
            <span class="multilang" lang="en">
                If \(f(x)= {@aa@}\) then we can write \( x =\displaystyle \frac{y-{@a1@}}{@a2@}\) and \( f^{-1}(x)= \displaystyle {@Ansa@}.\)
            </span>
            <span class="multilang" lang="de">
                Wenn \(f(x)= {@aa@}\) dann können wir schreiben \( x =\displaystyle \frac{y-{@a1@}}{@a2@}\) und \( f^{-1}(x)= \displaystyle {@Ansa@}.\)
            </span>
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <span class="multilang" lang="en">
                For \(f(x)= {@bb@}\) we take \( f^{-1}(x) = {@Ansb@}.\)
            </span>
            <span class="multilang" lang="de">
                Für \(f(x)= {@bb@}\) erhalten wir \( f^{-1}(x) = {@Ansb@}.\)
            </span>
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <span class="multilang" lang="en">
                For \(f(x)= {@cc@}\) we take \( f^{-1}(x) = \displaystyle {@Ansc@}.\)
            </span>
            <span class="multilang" lang="de">
                Für \(f(x)= {@cc@}\) erhalten wir \( f^{-1}(x) = \displaystyle {@Ansc@}. \)
            </span>
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <span class="multilang" lang="en">
                For \(\displaystyle{f(x)= {@dd@}}\) we take \( f^{-1}(x) =\displaystyle  {@Ansd@}.\)
            </span>
            <span class="multilang" lang="de">
                Für \(\displaystyle{f(x)= {@dd@}}\) erhalten wir \( f^{-1}(x) =\displaystyle  {@Ansd@}.\)
            </span>
        </p>
    </li>
</ol>
]]></text>
        </generalfeedback>
